※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=5
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ A local is a value, so one nothing refers to is an instruction nothing uses,
※ and an optimized build leaves nothing of it behind.  The program says the
※ same thing either way, which is what this checks.
let g: u8 = 3u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    @[ignore(4006)]
    let unread: u8 = g
    5u6
